Conclusion  : Good (provisional): lr_auprc=0.5755 is far above the ~0.11 random level named in the hypothesis. It is the first scored run, so is_new_best is True by default. No baseline score or best-so-far exists, so the Spearman-baseline part of the hypothesis cannot be checked. Secondary metrics support a real signal: lr_auroc 0.890 and direction_accuracy 0.821. Both health gates passed (10 distinct symbols, dominant tie fraction 0.103).
Key Factor  : Skip-anchored rank partial correlation with a very small head (385 params), trained with smooth_l1 for 10 epochs at trial_portion 1.0. The skip/partial-correlation structure most likely drives the score, not the head. No skip-only ablation was run, so the head's contribution is not separated.
Discovery   : The training dynamics are clean. Train loss fell from 0.0585 to 0.02219 and plateaued after about epoch 4. Validation fell from 0.0262 to 0.02188 and was best at epoch 9 (0.02184, in the 1-indexed checkpoint record; the dynamics line says best ep 8, which looks 0-indexed). Validation drifted only +4e-5 after the best epoch. The train-validation gap is about -3e-4, so validation is slightly below train. This shows no overfitting and no train-validation divergence. The loss is saturated from about epoch 5 onward, so more epochs on this config are unlikely to help. The 385-param head is not capacity-limited by anything these numbers show, but they also do not show it adds value over skip-only. The smooth_l1 loss values are the first of their type, so there is nothing to compare them with. Data volume is full (trial_portion 1.0), so the score is not a low-data artifact.
Memory Update: Record lr_auprc 0.5755 (auroc 0.890, dir_acc 0.821) as the reference for the skip-anchored rank-pcorr + small head config with smooth_l1, 10 epochs, 385 params. Next steps: (1) Run the skip-only ablation (no head, or a head initialised to identity) with the same seed and data. This resolves the hypothesis that the head gains under 0.02. (2) Run the Spearman baseline at the same portion so the 'at or above baseline' claim can be tested. (3) Do not spend effort on more epochs or lr tuning, because the loss plateaued by about epoch 5. If the head gain is negligible, prefer the skip-only variant as the more efficient candidate for solidification. Note that a forced formal round uses full portions of 1.0, so later comparisons should keep trial_portion 1.0 to stay comparable. Check seed variance, since only one seed has been run.
